WEBVTT

1
00:00:02.600 --> 00:00:03.300
You have a goal:

2
00:00:04.060 --> 00:00:05.560
fifteen percent more orders by March,

3
00:00:05.560 --> 00:00:07.240
at the same cost per order.

4
00:00:08.060 --> 00:00:08.720
A good goal.

5
00:00:09.600 --> 00:00:11.300
But how will you know you bought it?

6
00:00:13.900 --> 00:00:15.880
Four principles, before we plan anything.

7
00:00:19.280 --> 00:00:21.760
Principle one: measure whether the goals were met,

8
00:00:21.980 --> 00:00:23.060
do not only act.

9
00:00:24.320 --> 00:00:25.500
Activity is not evidence.

10
00:00:26.600 --> 00:00:27.780
If you cannot name the number

11
00:00:27.780 --> 00:00:28.840
that proves a goal happened,

12
00:00:29.220 --> 00:00:30.380
it was an aspiration.

13
00:00:33.380 --> 00:00:36.380
Principle two: measurement starts tactical and intuitive,

14
00:00:36.960 --> 00:00:38.500
then matures into precise insight.

15
00:00:39.640 --> 00:00:41.860
Nobody's first dashboard is right.

16
00:00:43.860 --> 00:00:46.060
Start measuring badly rather than not at all,

17
00:00:46.280 --> 00:00:47.360
and sharpen it every month.

18
00:00:52.760 --> 00:00:54.860
Principle three: understand what works,

19
00:00:55.180 --> 00:00:55.700
what does not,

20
00:00:55.700 --> 00:00:56.680
which campaign failed,

21
00:00:57.100 --> 00:00:58.360
and which investment was profitable.

22
00:00:59.420 --> 00:01:00.920
All four, not just the first.

23
00:01:01.500 --> 00:01:03.480
A plan that only reports successes

24
00:01:03.480 --> 00:01:05.180
cannot be optimised.

25
00:01:07.980 --> 00:01:10.540
Principle four: building the measurement infrastructure

26
00:01:10.540 --> 00:01:12.080
is a necessary step

27
00:01:12.080 --> 00:01:14.060
before any marketing activity begins.

28
00:01:15.220 --> 00:01:16.240
Set it up before the campaign.

29
00:01:17.220 --> 00:01:19.100
Nobody sets up tracking retroactively.

30
00:01:20.220 --> 00:01:21.780
Data you do not collect today

31
00:01:21.780 --> 00:01:23.960
cannot be analysed in the future.

32
00:01:27.460 --> 00:01:28.680
So before you spend anything,

33
00:01:29.120 --> 00:01:29.960
the tracking goes in.

34
00:01:31.120 --> 00:01:33.600
Now open your workbook: write your goal,

35
00:01:34.080 --> 00:01:36.000
and how and from when you will measure it.

